<title>USA: S.Africa gets first post-apartheid World Bank loan.</title>
<headline>S.Africa gets first post-apartheid World Bank loan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank said on Friday it would lend South Africa $46 million in its first loan to the country since Nelson Mandela took office in 1994.</p>
<p>The loan, the first to the country in over 30 years, will go to a government program to help medium, small and micro- enterprises compete internationally, the Bank said, adding it would be repaid over 15 years after a three-year grace period.</p>
</text>
